Checks: >
  clang-diagnostic-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  bugprone-*,
  cert-*,
  misc-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-*,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -readability-implicit-bool-conversion,
  -readability-uppercase-literal-suffix,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling

WarningsAsErrors: '*'

# Every suppression above was reached by running the enabled set against
# this directory, reading what came back, and fixing what was real (see
# hashutil.c/md5.h for the fixes that resulted: named digest-size
# constants, fclose/snprintf/fprintf return-value handling, a
# swappable-parameters fix in field(), a real int-overflow-into-pointer
# risk in md5.h's block/digest indexing). What's left is suppressed with
# a specific reason, not blanket-disabled:
#
# - readability-identifier-length: flags short loop/pointer names (i, j,
#   p, c, f, n, h) that are idiomatic and unambiguous in tight C scopes;
#   enforcing 3+ character names here would hurt readability, not help it.
# - readability-magic-numbers: fires on every literal in this file,
#   including the FIPS/RFC-mandated round constants, rotation amounts,
#   and K/H table entries in sha256.h/sha512.h/md5.h -- naming those
#   would be actively harmful (they ARE the spec, not something a future
#   maintainer should be tempted to "clean up"). The one place this check
#   was actually right -- hash-output buffer sizes that must track digest
#   sizes -- was fixed with named constants regardless of this suppression.
# - readability-implicit-bool-conversion: a C++-idiom check; in C, bool is
#   just an integer type and using it directly in a condition or as a
#   parameter (as this file does deliberately, e.g. `(algos & BIT) != 0`
#   passed as a `bool` parameter) is not a defect class here.
# - readability-uppercase-literal-suffix: `1412061192u` vs `1412061192U`
#   is pure style with no correctness implication; lowercase `u`/`ull` is
#   used consistently throughout this codebase (see murmur2.h, sha512.h).
# - clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling:
#   flags every snprintf/memcpy/memset call for not using C11 Annex K
#   `_s` variants, which glibc and mingw's runtime don't implement --
#   depending on them would make the code non-portable to the exact
#   platforms this tool targets.
